# Provisioning storage and pools in one apply

You can create the storage account, the access grants and the first pools in a single `terraform apply`. Call [terraform-azurerm-ipam](https://github.com/appvia/terraform-azurerm-ipam), feed its `provider_config` output to the provider, and make the pools depend on the module.

## Azure

{{ tffile "examples/single-apply/azure/main.tf" }}

## Why it works

- **The provider configuration must be known at plan time.** `provider_config` is built only from module inputs (account name and container), so it is. If you feed the provider a value that's only known after apply, planning fails with "Provider configuration is unknown".
- **`depends_on = [module.ipam]`** makes the pools wait for the container and the role assignments.
- **`access_propagation_timeout`** covers the delay before a new Azure role assignment takes effect. Creates retry access denied until it runs out (default `5m`).
- **Avoid `data.ipam_*` in the same first apply.** Data sources read at plan time, before the storage exists, and reads don't wait for access to propagate. Leave them out of the first apply or give them `depends_on = [module.ipam]` so the read is deferred to apply.
